Question : 
    Given a positive integer n, find the number of perfect squares that are less than n in the sample space of perfect squares. 
    The sample space consists of all perfect squares starting from 1 (i.e., 1, 4, 9, 16, 25, …)


Code : 
    class Solution {
        static int countSquares(int n) {
            // code here
            int count=0;
            for(int i=1; i*i<n; i++) {
                count++;
            }
            return count;
        }
    }


Time Complexity : O(Sqrt of n)
Space Complexity : O(1);


Explanation : 
    Here, we have to count number of perfect squares that are strictly less than n.
    So, we start from i and check i*i < n or not, if yes count increases otherwise loop terminates.
    Because once we find an i whose square is greater than n, the remaining sqaures will alsobe greater than n.